{
    "background_story": "Maverick was a majestic Andalusian stallion with a coat as black as coal and a mane that shone like the night sky. His owner, a skilled horse breeder, named him after the free-spirited cowboys of the American West. But Maverick's true claim to fame was his voice - he was a dulciana, a horse with a rare gift for producing a wide range of musical notes. When the breeder's daughter, a classically trained pianist, would play the piano in the stables, Maverick would respond with hauntingly beautiful whinnies, creating an impromptu duet that would mesmerize all who heard it. As word of the 'singing horse' spread, people would come from far and wide to hear Maverick's dulciana melodies, and the stallion would obligingly perform, his voice soaring like a celestial choir.",
